# SECTION 00 — MISSION OBJECTIVE

Your task is to transform the selected open-source pretrained ASR model into an Avapardaz-specialized speech recognition model.

The model must become significantly better suited to:

1. Iranian Persian speech.
2. Natural conversational Persian.
3. Formal Persian.
4. Persian-English code-switching.
5. English technical terminology.
6. Podcast and studio speech.
7. Telephone and low-bandwidth speech.
8. Different Persian speaking styles.
9. Multiple speakers and difficult acoustic conditions, where the selected model supports the required task.

The final model must remain deployable through the Central Avapardaz ASR Engine.

Production inference requirements:

```
LOCAL CPU INFERENCE
NO REQUIRED EXTERNAL AI API
NO CLOUD ASR DEPENDENCY
OFFLINE AFTER MODEL INSTALLATION
NO REQUIRED GPU FOR END USERS
CROSS-PLATFORM MODEL DELIVERY
```

Training and inference are separate workloads.

Training may require GPU acceleration.

The final trained model must be executable by the verified CPU inference runtimes selected in earlier phases.

Do not confuse the ability to train on GPU with a requirement for users to have GPUs.

The user's production computer must not need a GPU to transcribe audio.

